# Line-ending policy:
# - source and build files are stored and checked out with LF,
#   independent of the local core.autocrlf setting
# - Windows batch files are the exception: cmd.exe requires CRLF,
#   so they are stored with CRLF and never converted (-text)
# - test fixtures / corpora stay byte-exact (IGC etc. are CRLF by spec)
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd -text
*.bat -text
test/data/** -text
fuzzer/corpus/** -text
.settings/** -text
ide/eclipse/** -text
doc/manual/en/.project -text
doc/manual/figures/*.svg -text
